WEBVTT

00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:04.330
This investigation gives you boundary changes and asks you to predict

00:00:04.330 --> 00:00:07.530
the landscape. At the starting time, the west is a passive

00:00:07.530 --> 00:00:11.010
continental margin, with a small continental fragment offshore.

00:00:11.450 --> 00:00:15.370
The scenario then establishes eastward subduction beneath the main continent.

00:00:15.650 --> 00:00:19.350
In the east, a three-armed rift will separate another piece.

00:00:19.570 --> 00:00:23.750
These are specified conditions, not evidence that every real continent evolves

00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:24.370
this way.

00:00:24.940 --> 00:00:29.400
As the oceanic plate bends into subduction, predict a trench offshore.

00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:33.740
Scraped material can form an accretionary prism, with a forearc basin

00:00:33.740 --> 00:00:37.460
farther inland and a volcanic belt above the subduction system.

00:00:37.800 --> 00:00:40.800
The supplied thrust belt lies still farther inland.

00:00:41.180 --> 00:00:44.700
Its shortening thickens crust and builds mountains, while its load can

00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:47.820
produce a foreland basin in front of the advancing thrusts.

00:00:48.430 --> 00:00:52.050
Carry the small continental fragment toward the margin with the oceanic

00:00:52.050 --> 00:00:55.970
plate. Its buoyancy makes accretion and collision a reasonable prediction.

00:00:55.970 --> 00:00:59.510
It could enlarge and deform the continental edge, becoming a terrane.

00:00:59.730 --> 00:01:03.350
The precise final coastline is not uniquely determined by the sketch,

00:01:03.570 --> 00:01:06.850
so explain the mechanism rather than inventing an exact outline.

00:01:07.520 --> 00:01:10.900
On the eastern side, rifting thins the crust and lowers fault

00:01:10.900 --> 00:01:15.260
blocks while hotspot-related heating supports early uplift and volcanism.

00:01:15.520 --> 00:01:18.780
Two arms separate the continent and begin seafloor spreading.

00:01:19.040 --> 00:01:22.900
Later, the former hotspot is inactive and the continental edge cools

00:01:22.900 --> 00:01:24.680
and subsides into a passive margin.

00:01:24.920 --> 00:01:27.580
The spreading center has moved outside the diagram.

00:01:27.820 --> 00:01:30.860
A failed rift can remain as an inland low corridor.

00:01:31.570 --> 00:01:34.850
For the labeled sites, connect every predicted height change to a

00:01:34.850 --> 00:01:39.090
process. Magmatic additions and thrust stacking thicken crust;

00:01:39.390 --> 00:01:43.430
extension thins it; cooling increases density and promotes subsidence.

00:01:43.910 --> 00:01:47.730
At the western coast, local accretion and nearby basin formation can

00:01:47.730 --> 00:01:51.610
coexist, so avoid assigning one uniform response to the whole margin.

00:01:52.110 --> 00:01:54.950
Use the original figure's locations and requested symbols.

00:01:55.150 --> 00:01:58.770
This is a source-based reasoning model, not a supplied official answer

00:01:58.770 --> 00:01:59.050
key.
